THOUGHT: NullAway reports `action` as @Nullable, so calling `action.act(delta)` without a null-check is unsafe. The class already checks `if (action != null) action.restart();`, so it’s consistent to also guard the `act` call. I’ll modify `delegate(float)` to first check `action != null` before invoking `act`, preserving behavior (if `action` is null, the method just returns false and does nothing).

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '31,37c\    if (action != null && action.act(delta)) {
      if (finished) return true;
      if (repeatCount > 0) executedCount++;
      if (executedCount == repeatCount) return true;
      action.restart();
    }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/actions/RepeatAction.java
```

